WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.900
Fearless, relentless, and one of the most
utterly brutal warriors to ever walk the face

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.019
of the Earth, with a body count somewhere
in the high hundred thousands; if not well

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:15.500
into multiple millions given just how long
he’s been around for.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.660
Many of you will already be well aware of
SCP-076-2, also known as Able.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.439
On the surface, he’s a man of Middle Eastern
descent, covered in tattoos of occult symbols

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:29.590
and demonic faces.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:37.070
Usually contained within a stone cube designated
SCP-076-1, Able will often emerge in a homicidal

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.930
state, killing anyone and anything directly
around him.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:41.930
How?

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:47.469
Well, by any means available to him, but primarily
by pulling a wide array of bladed weapons

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:50.160
seemingly out of thin air.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.969
This is thanks to a tiny pocket dimension
that only he can reach into, which is also

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:59.940
always stocked with an assortment of deadly
implements for his latest murder spree.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.830
As if being highly combat proficient and always
armed didn’t make him enough of an imposing

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:12.369
threat, SCP-076-2 also possesses a near superhuman
resistance to damage, making him incredibly

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:14.350
difficult to take down.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.350
And even if someone is able to eventually
neutralize him, Able will also come back,

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:25.619
resurrecting inside SCP-076-1 to fight another
day.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:31.259
What you may not know is, for a time, Able
actually worked alongside the SCP Foundation.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:36.240
Although, nowadays, they prefer to keep him
locked away in a secure containment facility

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.220
underwater, which they will flood with seawater
if he ever escapes.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:46.060
But Able was once appointed the leader of
his own Mobile Task Force, Omega 7, referred

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.439
to under the codename of ‘Pandora’s Box’.

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:55.490
You see, the Foundation realized that SCP-076-2
held an especially high regard for those who

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.210
proved – well, able – to best him in combat.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:04.520
And it was this strange code of honor that
Able held that the Foundation hoped to exploit

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.020
with the creation of Pandora’s Box, comprised
of MTF operatives that had earned Able’s

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.660
respect, most by previously beating him in
a fair fight.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.000
Or as fair as a fight with a man who can summon
swords through a tear in the fabric of reality

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.360
can be.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:24.410
These agents would support Able during missions
in the field, during which the SCP Foundation

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.660
were able to deploy the anomalous warrior
in various tactical engagements.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:31.090
However, this didn’t last long.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.120
Eventually, Able grew tired of carrying out
the orders of the Foundation.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:41.190
The immortal warrior craved a challenge, breaking
free of containment and turning on the Foundation,

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.310
resulting in Able being neutralized by an
on-site nuclear weapon.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:52.440
This marked the end of the fragile alliance
between SCP-076-2 and the SCP Foundation,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.610
leaving the existence of Omega 7 a classified
secret, and one of the organization’s most

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.330
embarrassing missteps.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.250
But what if that hadn’t happened?

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:06.370
What if, out there in the infinite multiverse,
there was a world where Able had been allowed

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.870
to remain a part of Omega 7, and the Mobile
Task Force was never disbanded?

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.379
Well, you’re about to find out.

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:17.580
In our world, Able’s dissatisfaction with
being a member of Pandora’s Box first became

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.890
apparent when he began putting the rest of
his unit through live-fire exercises, brutalizing

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:28.670
his men despite these exercises being intended
as for training purposes only.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:34.341
But in this world, the injuries and even casualties
Able inflicted on the rest of Omega 7 were

00:03:34.341 --> 00:03:36.970
met with a much different response.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:42.760
The O5 Council of this alternate version of
the SCP Foundation, viewed Able’s outbursts

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.140
during training as acceptable losses.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:50.310
Every time he would injure one of Omega 7,
the Council would demand that replacements

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:55.940
be on hand to become part of the task force,
drawn from the ranks of the other MTFs at

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.470
their disposal.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:02.250
After all, Able was a valuable asset for carrying
out the Foundation’s dirty work.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.590
By continually replenishing his team with
reserves from their seemingly inexhaustible

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:14.480
supply of other MTF agents, the O5 Council
of this work were able to keep SCP-076-2 firmly

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.780
under their employ.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:20.500
However, it’s also important to note that
Able’s patience for these new recruits was

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.970
far more limited than the original Omega 7s.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:29.100
Those men had all been hand-picked by Able
personally and appointed to the project, given

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.100
that he had some modicum of respect for them
as combatants.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:38.140
Whereas all of their replacements were plucked
at random from the Foundation’s other MTFs.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:44.360
As a result, SCP-076-2 would carelessly kill
or wound more and more of these reserves during

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:49.010
combat missions, hardly distinguishing between
friend and foe.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:54.720
But despite this, the O5 Council refused to
discontinue the Omega 7 project, viewing these

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:00.230
as acceptable losses, and letting the success
rate of Able’s missions justify the depletion

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.949
of their other Mobile Task Forces.

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:08.120
Under Able’s leadership and the commands
of the O5 Council, Omega 7 would become this

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.500
Foundation’s primary rapid response unit
and the most deployed task force for dangerous

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.979
field operations.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:18.800
And working for the Foundation meant that
every field mission was a highly dangerous

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.800
one.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.569
Such was the case during one containment breach
where SCP-682 managed to get free of its acid

00:05:25.569 --> 00:05:26.569
tank.

00:05:26.569 --> 00:05:30.919
A rampaging, infinitely adaptable Hard to
Destroy Reptile on the loose, slaughtering

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:32.960
all in its path, was bad enough.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.810
But the O5 Council had received intel that
there was something more behind this breakout

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.470
than it first seemed.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:45.979
And so, Able and the rest of his latest Omega
7 team were sent in to pacify SCP-682.

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:52.100
Bursting into the facility, eager to once
again be freed from containment and the monotonous,

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.610
underwhelming experience of training, Able
flew into combat.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:01.569
Drawing black swords from his personal armory,
he began to tear through everything and everyone

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:03.009
in his path.

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:07.250
Unfortunately, for the Foundation personnel
on site, this also meant they were subject

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:09.580
to Able’s relentless wrath.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:14.810
As if running away from SCP-682 wasn’t bad
enough, fleeing research staff were quickly

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:21.500
met with the swing of SCP-076-2’s weapons,
and removed from the premises in a brutal

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.500
fashion.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.729
Still, this meant little to Able, and even
less to the O5 Council.

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:31.200
As far as they were concerned, even their
own staff were just collateral damage, more

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:36.690
acceptable losses justified by Able’s perfect
record for successful, high-risk, high-reward

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.940
field missions.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:41.849
However, that perfect record was about to
be tarnished for good…

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:47.599
You see, this containment breach wasn’t
your average SCP-682 escape attempt.

00:06:47.599 --> 00:06:53.040
It was instead a situation that had been meticulously
planned and carried out for one purpose.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:57.039
This breach was intended specifically to draw
Able out.

00:06:57.039 --> 00:07:01.280
Since he had become the SCP Foundation’s
primary weapon and response to danger in the

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:06.030
field, a particularly devious third party
had begun to take note.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:11.120
The Chaos Insurgency, a splinter faction that
began its life as an off-the-books black ops

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:16.410
unit for the Foundation themselves, had been
monitoring Able’s deployment by the O5 Council.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:21.889
In this universe, their origin was the same
as in ours, and the Insurgency took a certain

00:07:21.889 --> 00:07:27.020
disdain to seeing an anomalous individual
carrying out the kind of operations their

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.240
group had been formed to undertake for the
Foundation.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:38.110
Additionally, the use of SCP-076-2 as a personal
attack dog by the O5 Council is hypocrisy.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:43.259
The Insurgency believed in the practical application
of anomalies rather than locking them up and

00:07:43.259 --> 00:07:47.900
keeping them contained, and it was for this
belief that they had been vilified by the

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.900
Foundation.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:55.210
And yet, here was the same organization, sending
Able on missions, with no care for the harm

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.660
he caused.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:01.440
And so, as a result, the Chaos Insurgency
had conducted an operation to break into the

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:08.510
Foundation, free SCP-682 and send the Hard
to Destroy Reptile on a rampage, all so they

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:11.240
could take their shot at Able.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:17.340
Being ambushed by a group of Chaos Insurgency
operatives on his way to engage SCP-682, Able

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.629
was admittedly caught by surprise.

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:24.340
But by now, his combat prowess was second
to almost nobody else in the world.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:28.650
The Insurgents dogpiled on Able, unleashing
every ounce of firepower they had brought

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.810
to bear on the immortal warrior.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:35.599
The ensuing firefight destroyed an entire
wing of the Foundation facilities, explosive

00:08:35.599 --> 00:08:40.160
weapons being detonated in the hopes that
the Insurgency could subdue Able.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:46.260
All the while, SCP-076-2 shrugged off the
oncoming damage, catching rockets that were

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.769
launched at him and throwing them back in
the direction of the Chaos Insurgents.

00:08:50.769 --> 00:08:56.830
It was a bloodbath, nearly the entire Omega
7 team that had been accompanying Able and

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.690
providing him with fire support were lying
dead.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:04.220
The same could also be said for the Insurgency
forces too, though, with each of them being

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:07.130
gradually felled by the warrior's many weapons.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:13.030
But by this point, Able was approaching exhaustion,
and there was still one more enemy left standing.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:18.050
It had been unfurling destruction all of its
own, angrily devouring the few Foundation

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.370
personnel that were left.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:24.950
And now, the scaly form of SCP-682 came lumbering
around the corner.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:29.700
The battle was brutal; in this universe, Able
and the Hard to Destroy Reptile had never

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.570
crossed paths before.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:36.360
But SCP-682 could smell the difference in
Able’s physiology, his innate ability to

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.380
resist damage and resurrect time and time
again.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:44.130
The creature already held disdain for anything
and everything living, and so, presented with

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:51.220
a man who technically couldn’t stop living,
SCP-682 entered an unstoppable rage state,

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.029
taking the exhausted Able down with ease.

00:09:54.029 --> 00:09:59.640
But losing in a grudge match against SCP-682
wasn’t quite as bad as things were about

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.120
to get for Able.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:06.800
Reviving inside his stone cube, the ancient
warrior was confused; the Foundation weren’t

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:07.800
letting him out.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:13.380
It had been a long time, years even, since
he had last ‘died’ even temporarily.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:18.360
Over the course of all his Omega 7 missions,
he hadn’t needed to reappear back inside

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.280
SCP-076-1 for quite a considerable while.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:27.080
And now that he had, a very large seed of
doubt had been sown.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:33.660
The O5 Council were furious, just as angry
at SCP-076-2’s apparent failure as Able

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.660
was.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:39.329
The perfect operational track record of their
top anomalous asset was now tarnished.

00:10:39.329 --> 00:10:43.269
The question started to spread through the
council members; if their sword-wielding,

00:10:43.269 --> 00:10:48.070
virtually invulnerable secret weapon wasn’t
as effective as they had previously thought,

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:51.589
then what was the use of continuing to deploy
Able?

00:10:51.589 --> 00:10:58.279
And so began a debate within the O5 Council,
upon what was to be the fate of SCP-076-2.

00:10:58.279 --> 00:11:03.700
In this universe, he had served the Foundation
well, but a weapon that is only effective

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:07.500
even 90% of the time still leaves a margin
of error.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:12.700
It was that risk, that potential for error,
knowing that Able wouldn’t always succeed

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:18.320
in his missions, that caused the O5 Council
to reconsider his applications as a field

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.320
operative.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.630
There were some in the Council who argued
that this was a highly specific, isolated

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:24.630
incident.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:30.660
The Chaos Insurgency had specifically engineered
the SCP-682 escape as a way to draw Able out,

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.779
after all.

00:11:31.779 --> 00:11:35.790
Just because he had failed this time didn’t
indicate a pattern of failure.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:40.230
But this argument was eventually shot down,
especially when the Foundation’s Ethics

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.060
Committee decided to throw in their two cents.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:48.300
They demanded Able’s status as a field agent
be revoked, and levied for the immediate disbanding

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.160
of the Omega 7 project.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:54.470
Pooling replacements for that task force from
other MTFs at the Foundation had left them

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:57.940
with a significantly depleted reserve of troops.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:02.420
And then came the argument about just how
‘acceptable’ the losses were whenever

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.550
Able was let loose.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:10.880
A decision was ultimately made to – at least
for the moment – rescind SCP-076-2’s field

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:16.829
operative privileges and suspend any further
deployment of or recruitment into Omega 7.

00:12:16.829 --> 00:12:21.519
However, there was one crucial factor that
nobody on the Council had taken into consideration

00:12:21.519 --> 00:12:27.350
when they made their verdict: and that was
how badly Able would react to the news.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:32.510
As you may already have predicted, Able was
furious to hear he would be held in containment

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:34.190
until further notice.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:39.529
His anger stemmed not only from his defeat
at the jaws of SCP-682, but at how quick the

00:12:39.529 --> 00:12:42.769
Foundation seemingly was to question his combat
prowess.

00:12:42.769 --> 00:12:47.890
He’d lost one battle out of hundreds – thousands
even – and all of a sudden the O5 Council

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:49.550
were going to lock him away?

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.420
All because of one defeat?

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:52.999
“You dare!”

00:12:52.999 --> 00:12:54.660
Able bellowed when he was given the news.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:13:00.130
“I am the greatest warrior on this planet,
and have been made a pawn by your Foundation.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:05.670
I give you my strength, my skill, and the
moment I falter, you turn your back on me?

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:06.680
You dare?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.690
YOU DARE?!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:11.660
I WILL SHOW YOU WHAT REAL POWER LOOKS LIKE!”

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:16.279
Overcome with rage, it didn’t take long
for Able to force his way out of containment.

00:13:16.279 --> 00:13:20.930
He’d been active as a field agent within
the Foundation for so long now that he had

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:25.700
long since figured out a way to escape his
underwater prison before the emergency containment

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.990
measures had a chance to stop him.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:31.980
As he broke free, he made sure to take down
plenty of security staff on the way.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:35.810
And to make matters worse, he didn’t stop
there.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:39.519
Before long, Able was on the warpath against
the SCP Foundation.

00:13:39.519 --> 00:13:43.139
Every few days, reports would come in of a
massacre at a Foundation facility.

00:13:43.139 --> 00:13:48.210
Security footage recovered from the wreckage
after each incident would show Able arriving

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:51.410
primed for battle, a sword in each hand.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:56.170
By the time he left after his brutal, remorseless
attack, he’d be drenched in the blood of

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.279
the entire Site’s personnel.

00:13:58.279 --> 00:14:02.330
The Foundation had little in its once huge
arsenal to fight back with.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:07.769
Given the number of MTF agents reassigned
to Omega 7, their forces were far more limited,

00:14:07.769 --> 00:14:09.399
if not almost depleted.

00:14:09.399 --> 00:14:13.810
They dispatched attachments to clean up the
wake of Able’s destruction, but not one

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:17.360
squad sent after the anomalous warrior came
back alive.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:22.800
Part of the problem was, the Foundation couldn’t
predict where Able would show up next, or

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:26.100
which of their Sites he knew about and was
planning to hit.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:31.529
From their perspective, his attacks were spontaneous,
the result of rage at the Foundation, but

00:14:31.529 --> 00:14:34.140
without any premeditated plan in mind.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.209
And that was exactly what Able wanted them
to think.

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:43.060
By seeming to attack at random, he was, therefore,
able to cover the true intention behind each

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:46.480
engagement: he was looking for something.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.310
During his considerable time leading Omega
7, he had heard about a machine that could

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:57.029
improve anything placed inside it: SCP-914,
better known as the Clockworks.

00:14:57.029 --> 00:15:01.000
And before long, Able found what he was looking
for.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.759
By the time the Foundation realized what the
unstoppable warrior’s plan was, it was already

00:15:05.759 --> 00:15:06.970
too late.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:12.800
Able was storming into the facility that housed
SCP-914, with no intention of leaving until

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:13.820
he’d used it.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:18.550
The Foundation had banned testing of biological
matter within the Clockworks, but Able wasn’t

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.279
beholden to their rules anymore.

00:15:20.279 --> 00:15:24.670
In fact, he barely was when he’d worked
with them before.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:29.610
Cutting down guards and researchers, survivors
fleeing in terror, Able stepped up towards

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.470
the mass of gears and cogs, the clockwork
components that made up SCP-914.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:39.100
He wasted no time, setting the machine to
‘Very Fine’.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:42.910
With this setting, the Clockworks would take
whatever was in its Input booth and improve

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:45.600
it, usually by giving it anomalous properties.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:51.070
Or, in the case of Able, by giving him further
anomalous properties.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:56.040
Stepping inside, the whirr of machinery drowned
out the emergency alarms, as Able reached

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:03.459
his goal… to become the ultimate warrior,
the embodiment of the very concept itself.

00:16:03.459 --> 00:16:06.680
Racing to the scene, a chopper cleared the
smoke as it approached.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:11.230
Under an emergency executive order from the
O5 Council, the few surviving remnants of

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:15.620
the Foundation’s Mobile Task Forces had
been combined into a singular strike team.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.860
There weren’t many left, considering how
many others from their units had been previously

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:26.420
siphoned into Omega 7, only to die as collateral
damage in that team’s missions with Able.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.420
“Remember, SCP-076-2 is a priority target!”

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.350
the field commander barked, while the MTF
strike team held their guns nervously aboard

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:35.350
the aircraft.

00:16:35.350 --> 00:16:39.209
“Primary objective is to neutralize him
by any means.

00:16:39.209 --> 00:16:43.870
Reports indicate that he may be trying to
access SCP-914, so be advised-”

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:49.040
An almighty explosion boomed through the airborne
vehicle, engulfing the cockpit in flames.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.760
“Mayday, mayday; Chopper One has been hit,
we are going down!!”

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.069
the commander radioed to Foundation command.

00:16:55.069 --> 00:16:57.540
“Everyone brace yourselves for impact.”

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:02.360
The helicopter spiraled out of the air, crashing
to the ground in a twisted hunk of metal.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:06.520
The surviving members of the strike team scrabbled
out of the wreckage, hauling the more badly

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.699
wounded out of the ruined aircraft.

00:17:08.699 --> 00:17:09.699
“Contact!”

00:17:09.699 --> 00:17:10.789
someone yelled in horror.

00:17:10.789 --> 00:17:13.079
“Enemy contact behind us!”

00:17:13.079 --> 00:17:17.419
The remaining Foundation foot soldiers turned
and drew their weapons, opening fire on something

00:17:17.419 --> 00:17:20.169
suspended a few feet in the air above them.

00:17:20.169 --> 00:17:25.760
A hail of gunfire rang out, as the team opened
fire the second that they saw who it was…

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:29.059
it was Able, and he was flying.

00:17:29.059 --> 00:17:33.200
Floating above them, his hair whipping in
the wind, the oncoming storm of bullets seemed

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.940
to ricochet off his skin.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:39.320
In actuality, they weren’t even hitting
him; melting away before they could make contact.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:44.070
They might as well have been firing pea shooters
for how little effect their guns had.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:47.720
The barrage only stopped when one of the strike
team launched a short-range rocket at the

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.309
newly refined warrior.

00:17:49.309 --> 00:17:53.570
It detonated, but when the smoke from the
blast cleared, Able was still hovering in

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.340
the air, without so much as a scratch.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.130
“My turn,” he announced.

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:03.870
Reaching into his pocket dimension, Able pulled
something out: not a weapon, not yet.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:09.340
Instead, it was a formless, dark, shadowy
mass, that moved like liquid metal, reacting

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.200
to the movement of his hand.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.660
As he drew the substance out, it reformed,
seemingly at Able’s command.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:18.250
And it wasn’t just swords he could create
now.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.890
Drawing on his experiences from his Omega
7 missions, any weapon that Able had previously

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:27.010
seen or could think of, he now had at his
disposal.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:31.860
The strike team looked up in horror as a veritable
swarm of black, non-reflective constructs

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:36.669
hovered in the air on either side of Able;
each one in the shape of a rocket.

00:18:36.669 --> 00:18:39.060
Flinging both arms toward the Foundation troops.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.860
Able sent his new creations raining down on
them.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:46.400
The strike team turned heel and fled for their
lives, although none of them got very far.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:51.100
Able’s rockets engulfed the area around
them in a volley of explosions, leaving not

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.550
a single living thing standing.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:58.070
He had just effortlessly built an airstrike
from virtually thin air and thrown it at the

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:02.830
Foundation’s last remaining MTF agents…
and he wasn’t done there.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:07.210
With his newfound powers, Able’s campaign
of destruction swept the entire world.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:12.340
In a last act of desperation, the SCP Foundation
offered freedom to any anomaly that permanently

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:15.640
took down SCP-076-2.

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:20.470
They all flooded out of containment to take
their shot, the Plague Doctor, the Shy Guy,

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:24.090
The Specter… and they barely slowed Able
down.

00:19:24.090 --> 00:19:29.480
His new constructs were devastating weapons,
taking the form of not just blades, but projectiles

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.070
of every size and shape; all of them lethal.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:35.809
Before long, Able had lain waste to the entire
Foundation.

00:19:35.809 --> 00:19:38.730
But still, he wanted more.

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:44.039
SCP-914 hadn’t just improved Able’s existing
anomalous powers and granted him the ability

00:19:44.039 --> 00:19:49.340
to fly at supersonic speeds, but in doing
so, had amplified his rage too.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:55.450
He loathed the human race, and sought to absolutely
decimate every single living thing.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:20:01.110
No one could best him in combat now, and in
his mind, twisted by anger, not one of them

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:02.870
was worthy of his respect.

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:08.540
He tore planes apart with his bare hands,
smashed tanks to pieces, and leveled entire

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:11.290
cities with his unlimited weapons.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.230
It took a few years, maybe a decade at the
most.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:20.260
But by the end of it, Able was sat atop a
pile of billions upon billions of bones.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:26.170
With his refined abilities, he had done something
unthinkable: committed omnicide.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:28.830
He had killed everyone in the world.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:33.540
Of course, this was indeed another world,
one different to ours.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:37.450
Luckily, here, our version of Able is still
locked up underwater.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:43.450
But somewhere out there, the is an Able who
is watching the sun rising over an entirely

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.790
dead world.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:45.790
His world.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.290
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:52.260
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:56.621
Now to see the result of more anomalous experiments
with the Clockworks, go and check out “WHAT

00:20:56.621 --> 00:21:00.920
IF SCP-096 WAS PUT INSIDE SCP-914?”

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:06.120
and “SCP-914 WHAT DID YOU PUT IN IT?!”

